Scion: no Apple implementation-defined registers on a non-Apple CPU.

Modifications to Apple's xnu (xnu-12377.121.6) and new files for it, Apple Public
Source License 2.0 (APSL-2.0); see https://www.opensource.apple.com/apsl/. Original
files: Apple Inc. These changes: Scion contributors. Apply in order after buildfix.sh.

SCION_NATIVE_PAC builds only. NO_CPU_OVRD (as on the Apple SoCs that already set it),
and the CPU-shutdown loop no longer writes Apple's IPI register S3_5_C15_C1_1, which a
Cortex core under KVM or QEMU UNDEFs.

diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines_asm.s b/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines_asm.s
index f72582f..d5fe8bf 100644
--- a/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines_asm.s
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines_asm.s
@@ -1663,7 +1663,7 @@ Lwfi_inst:
 	dsb		sy
 	isb		sy
 	wfi
-#if NO_CPU_OVRD
+#if NO_CPU_OVRD && !SCION_NO_APPLE_IMPDEF_REGS
 	// Clear any spurious IPIs received during CPU shutdown
 	mov     x9, #0x1
 	msr     S3_5_C15_C1_1, x9
diff --git a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/VMAPPLE.h b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/VMAPPLE.h
index e531c28..ef40294 100644
--- a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/VMAPPLE.h
+++ b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/VMAPPLE.h
@@ -44,6 +44,8 @@
  * registers itself (see SCION_NATIVE_PAC in arm64/pac_asm.h). The keys are
  * one set per boot, shared by EL0 and EL1: there are no per-process keys.
  */
+#define NO_CPU_OVRD                1 /* a non-Apple CPU has no CPU_OVRD ... */
+#define SCION_NO_APPLE_IMPDEF_REGS 1 /* ... and no Apple implementation-defined registers */
 #else
 #define HAS_PARAVIRTUALIZED_PAC   1
 #endif
